#
# The public SSH key that signs every OAK Community release after 0.9.0 (RR-005), in the
# `ssh-keygen -Y` allowed-signers format: one line, `<principal> <key type> <public key>`.
# `scripts/verify_release.py` checks `SHA256SUMS.sig` against this file and nothing else.
# Consumers take it from the default branch, not a release's tag, so removing a revoked
# key here stops every release it signed from verifying; a rotated key keeps its line.
#
# No key is pinned yet: the maintainer generates the key, keeps the private half offline
# and adds the public line here before the first signed release is tagged
# (docs/release-process.md). Until then no release after 0.9.0 can verify, which is the
# point.
